// =====================================================================
// C64 MINE DEMAKE - 1_charset.ms   (GENERATED by tools/genchars.py)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// The 256-glyph MULTICOLOR CHAR ROM. One look for the whole game:
// every tile, item, creature and letter is an 8x8 cell of double-wide
// pixels, like the C64's multicolor charset mode.
//
// Each glyph is 32 digits = 8 rows x 4 columns. Digit = ink:
//   0 = common background (sky/border, shared by all cells)
//   1 = shared highlight ink (white)
//   2 = per-cell ACCENT color (color RAM)
//   3 = per-cell MAIN color   (color RAM)
// i.e. 2 free colors per char + a common background (plus white).
//
// You can ALSO edit the art without touching code: open the sprite
// "charrom" in microStudio's sprite editor (sprites/charrom.png).
// Each 8x8 cell of that sheet is one glyph, in reading order; use the
// 4 role colors  black/white/red/cyan  for inks 0/1/2/3 (exact VIC-II
// values). If that sprite exists, the game loads glyphs from it.
// =====================================================================

